Parse bookmark HTML in the browser process on HarmonyOS.

Importing a bookmarks file needs Chromium's Netscape-format parser. In 154 it
runs behind a mojo service in a utility process, and a HarmonyOS phone is
denied native child processes by the platform, so it runs single-process and
has no utility process to launch. ParseBookmarksUnsafe is the same parser
without the service, so chrome/browser calls it directly.

Favicon decoding is the one part that genuinely needs a child process: it
calls content::DecodeImage, which decodes with blink, and the browser process
does not initialize blink. It is skipped on OHOS; bookmarks import without
their stored icons and Chromium refetches them on first visit.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

